# The factory embeds `contracts/BountyClaim.py` byte-for-byte into
# `contracts/BountyRegistry.py`, and what studionet stores for the registry and
# for every deployed child is exactly those bytes (the corrected contracts were
# bundled and redeployed from Linux, so they carry LF). Normalising line endings
# on commit/checkout would change the embedded payload, break
# `scripts/build_bundle.py --check`, and break the byte-exact "the chain stores
# this file" check in `scripts/verify_explorer_evidence.py`. So these files are
# stored verbatim.
*.py -text
*.pyc binary

# Evidence is machine-generated output; compare it byte-for-byte, never rewrite it.
evidence/*.json -text
evidence/*.txt -text

# Docs are safe to normalise.
*.md text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
